          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is ALOHA protein powder healthy?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most people, yes: it is USDA Organic and Non-GMO Project Verified, with 5 g of fiber, 7 mg of iron in the chocolate, no artificial sweeteners and no stevia or sugar alcohols. The caveats are 4 g of added coconut sugar and a modest 18 g of protein. Anyone with kidney disease or a medical condition should ask a doctor first."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does ALOHA protein powder contain stevia or erythritol?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. ALOHA protein powder is sweetened with organic coconut sugar and organic monk fruit extract, and ALOHA says it never uses stevia, sucralose, aspartame or sugar alcohols such as erythritol, maltitol, xylitol or sorbitol. It also says its monk fruit contains no erythritol. The trade-off is 4 g of added sugar per serving."
