              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming organic means tested for heavy metals</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                USDA Organic covers farming and handling, not contaminants. ALOHA says it tests each product for lead, cadmium, mercury and arsenic, but it does not publish the results. If metals are your main concern, favor brands that post lot certificates, and do not treat the organic seal as proof.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Mixing it with plain water and expecting a thick shake</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
