                <p>
                  ALOHA sells only chocolate and vanilla. Based on buyer and reviewer feedback, chocolate is the safer choice: the cocoa and cinnamon cover the slight coconut note that one independent reviewer disliked in the vanilla. Vanilla has less sodium (250 mg vs 320 mg) and works well in fruit smoothies, where its milder sweetness helps. Both cost the same.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are the common complaints about ALOHA protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The complaints reviewers mention are a thin texture when mixed with water, a slight coconut aftertaste and a modest protein dose for the price. Some also find it less sweet than mainstream powders, which others count as a positive. The small 15-serving canister means frequent reorders, and the brand-site price is notably higher than Amazon's.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is ALOHA protein powder good for weight loss?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It can fit a weight-loss diet: 130 calories, 18 g of protein and 5 g of fiber per serving help a shake feel filling for its calories. Note that the label itself says to use it as a food supplement only and not for weight reduction. No powder causes weight loss by itself, so count it within your daily calories and protein.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

